      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "In keeping with its tradition, Aga Khan University (AKU) celebrated Independence Day on August 14, 2001. The chief guest, Mr. Jameel Yusuf, Chief, Citizen-Police Liaison Committee (CPLC), urged citizens to work in areas of health, education and law and order, and lauded AKU for being an institution \"that reflects the Islamic way of existence.\" Felicitating the jubilant guests on the nation's 54th birth anniversary, Dr. Shamsh Kassim-Lakha, President, AKU, suggested focus on human resources and underlined the importance of research in dealing with problems facing society."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
